                                    <h1>AI Content Moderation for Platforms: Guide 2026</h1>
                                    <p>Every platform that accepts user-generated content — social, marketplace, community, dating, gaming — needs content moderation infrastructure. Scale forces AI. Regulation (DSA in EU, IT Rules in India) forces documented processes. Here is what modern content moderation looks like end-to-end.</p>
                                    <h2>The Content Moderation Stack</h2>
                                    <ol><li><strong>Ingestion + classification</strong> — every piece of UGC scored on category, risk.</li><li><strong>Automated actions</strong> — high-confidence removals (CSAM, terrorism, doxxing).</li><li><strong>Review queue</strong> — mid-confidence items to human moderators.</li><li><strong>User reporting</strong> — community flagging of missed content.</li><li><strong>Appeal process</strong> — mandatory under DSA and most modern regulations.</li><li><strong>Transparency reporting</strong> — quarterly public reports.</li><li><strong>Regulatory reporting</strong> — CSAM to NCMEC, terrorism to relevant authorities.</li></ol>
                                    <h2>AI Model Layer</h2>
                                    <p><strong>Image / video:</strong> Hive, Sightengine, Amazon Rekognition, Google Vision. CSAM detection: PhotoDNA (mandatory partnership for most platforms).<br><strong>Text:</strong> Perspective API (Google), Hive Text, custom LLM-based classifiers.<br><strong>Audio:</strong> emerging (Whisper + classification).<br><strong>LLM for context:</strong> nuanced cases (sarcasm, satire, cultural context) benefit from LLM review.</p>
                                    <h2>Regulatory Requirements</h2>
                                    <p><strong>EU DSA:</strong> transparency reports, appeal process, notice-and-action, risk assessment (VLOPs).<br><strong>USA:</strong> Section 230 protections + CSAM reporting to NCMEC. State-level variations.<br><strong>UK:</strong> Online Safety Act 2023 — duties of care.<br><strong>India:</strong> IT Rules 2021 + amendments. Grievance officer required.<br><strong>Australia:</strong> Online Safety Act 2021, eSafety Commissioner.<br><strong>UAE:</strong> Digital communication regulations, TRA guidance.</p>
                                    <h2>Human Moderator Ops</h2>
                                    <p>Even at massive AI accuracy, human moderators handle 5-15% of content — edge cases + appeals. Structure: internal team OR BPO partner (Accenture, Genpact, Cognizant offer content moderation services). Attention to wellness / burnout critical (repeat exposure to harmful content).</p>
                                    <h2>Cost + Timeline</h2>
                                    <p><strong>Off-shelf integration (Hive / Sightengine / Perspective):</strong> ₹15-40 lakh / $18K-48K + per-scan / per-1K API costs.<br><strong>Custom moderation platform:</strong> ₹60 lakh - 2 Cr / $72K-240K.<br><strong>Enterprise multi-modal (image + video + text + audio):</strong> ₹2-6 Cr / $240K-720K.<br>Ongoing per-content moderation cost: $0.0005-0.005 per item at scale.</p>

